.TH SCHEMA-REVERSE 1 "2026 July 10" "Qore 3.0" "Qore Programming Language"
.SH NAME
schema\-reverse \- compatibility alias for qschema export
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B schema\-reverse
[\fIoptions\fP]
\fIconnection\fP
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBschema\-reverse\fR invokes \fBqschema export\fR with the same arguments.
It is retained for compatibility with existing scripts; new scripts should
use \fBqschema export\fR directly.
.PP
The command reverse-engineers a database into a complete Qore data-schema
document in YAML (\fB.ysm\fP) or JSON (\fB.jsm\fP) format.
It is read-only and supports selecting object types or name patterns.
.SH OPTIONS
See \fBqschema\fR(1), particularly the \fBExport Options\fR section, for the
complete option list.
.SH EXAMPLES
Export the full schema to a YAML file:
.RS
.B schema\-reverse \-s MySchema pgsql:user/pass@db \-o myschema.ysm
.RE
.PP
Equivalent canonical command:
.RS
.B qschema export \-s MySchema pgsql:user/pass@db \-o myschema.ysm
.RE
